@node Wigner d-matrix
@subsection Wigner d-matrix

@deftypefun double gsl_sf_wigner_drot (int @var{two_j}, int @var{two_m1}, int @var{two_m2}, double @var{theta})
@deftypefunx int gsl_sf_wigner_drot_e (int @var{two_j}, int @var{two_m1}, int @var{two_m2}, double @var{theta}, gsl_sf_result * @var{result})
These routines compute the Wigner (small) d-matrix element
@tex
\beforedisplay
$$
d^{j}_{m_1 m_2}(\theta) = \langle j m_1 | e^{-i \theta J_y} | j m_2 \rangle
$$
\afterdisplay
@end tex
@ifinfo

@example
d^j_{m1 m2}(theta) = <j m1| exp(-i theta Jy) |j m2>
@end example

@end ifinfo
@noindent
where the angular momenta are given in half-integer units, @math{j} =
@var{two_j}/2, @math{m_1} = @var{two_m1}/2, @math{m_2} =
@var{two_m2}/2, and @var{theta} is the rotation angle in radians.  The
value is computed from the finite sum of Zare, Eq. 3.57.  An error is
returned if @math{j < 0}, @math{|m_1| > j}, @math{|m_2| > j} or
@math{j + m_1} and @math{j + m_2} are not integers.
@comment Exceptional Return Values: GSL_EDOM
@end deftypefun

